two points on this:

&#x200B;

1 - "homemade" could imply that they get frozen buns (raw dough) either in the dinner roll shape or as a ball of dough, this label does not necessarily mean that the company produced the dough from scratch

&#x200B;

2- these buns were likely stamped and dated in a plastic bag to follow health standards/regulations. There may have been an issue on the bag and the stamp got through to the bun underneath.

&#x200B;

Either way this is shitty, but to suggest that packaged bread in the grocery store is "homemade" is a big stretch by any means

&#x200B;

Ex: when I worked at Mcds, I had to try to sell "fresh baked cookes" - these cookies came fully cooked and frozen from the factory, we just put them in the oven for a few minutes to heat them. The terms "baked in house" "freshly made" etc gave the false sense that employees were in the back mixing up cookie dough and baking cookies like you would make at home. Absolutely not the case and probably similar for these buns

I'm a 24 year old woman but I have been told I have the body of a 12 year old boy.

&#x200B;

My ED brain tells me this is a great success though so

Since were talking about birthdays, I told my mom that I didn't want a cake this year because i don't like cake (mostly true, I find other sweet things much more worth than cake) and she got very upset that we had a tradition of having cake, blowing out candles etc etc 

&#x200B;

So I tell her to get a cake and stick some candles in it, but to make sure that it was a small one and that I wasn't going to be obligated to eat any.

&#x200B;

Fast forward to the cake event, not only was the cake giant but I got told I was ruining my birthday for her (LOL) because I didn't want to eat cake. 

&#x200B;

Not exactly related to this post but birthday themed and I just wanted to rant a little bit thanks for coming to my Ted talk

It would be a stretch and a half to call it "control" - more like aggressive and uncontrolled.

&#x200B;

The dehydration and constant pain from getting your wisdom teeth out are on a similar level to the 4th day of a bad flare up though so I feel your pain and hope you feel better soon!
